m427Dll: the hit boxes' unused y starts as zero, not uninitialised stack, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

ADR 0008, "Gate status after the implementation", decision point 1 (the seed 2 split). m427Dll's
map.c builds hit boxes in local Vecs and passes them by value to fn_1_15F10 and fn_1_15FD0
(player.c), which copy them into lbl_1_bss_57C's records in a HuMem block. fn_1_7C34, fn_1_7F38 and
fn_1_8768 set only x and z; y is never written, so the records got whatever the stack held there. On
PC that included the low half of a pointer into the module (seqPunctTbl's address), which moved with
the module layout and split the layout probe's trail on seed 2 at frame 70,499. The records' y is
never read (the hit tests and the debug draw use x and z only), so this changes no behaviour: y is
now zero on every platform. Unconditional on PC.

